      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Most standard policies cover disruptive or unpredictable behavior under general misconduct terms like \"unauthorized absence\" or \"unprofessional conduct,\" provided you can document specific instances of the behavior. Since these actions may not always constitute a direct policy violation, it becomes critical to document every interaction with dates and details to create a clear pattern of incompetence or insubordination. Before proceeding with formal discipline, ensure you have attempt to address the behavior immediately with the employee to confirm the company's concern.",
